Package: inconsistency-by-hymy
Architecture: i386
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 libsdl1.2debian
Description: 1k intro for Linux, released in 2013
 Inconsistency is a 1 kilobyte intro by Hymy, released at Assembly 2013
 (11th in the PC 1k compo): a software rendered strange attractor with
 synthesized music.
 .
 The intro is a self-extracting shell script: a gzipped 32-bit ELF
 executable, written in assembly, is extracted into a temporary directory
 and run with SDL 1.2. On amd64, install the i386 version of the package
 (multiarch).
